#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM gratis tentang informasi dan komputasi kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical formulations of measurements"
msgstr "Formulasi matematis dari pengukuran"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore biggr Biggr operatorname */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore biggr Biggr operatorname */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The lesson begins with two equivalent mathematical descriptions of measurements:\n"
msgstr "Pelajaran ini dimulai dengan dua deskripsi matematis pengukuran yang setara:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "General measurements can be described by *collections of matrices*, one for each measurement outcome, in a way that generalizes the description of projective measurements.\n"
msgstr "Pengukuran umum bisa dijelaskan melalui *kumpulan matriks*, satu untuk setiap hasil pengukuran, dengan cara yang menggeneralisasi deskripsi pengukuran proyektif.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "General measurements can be described as *channels* whose outputs are always classical states (represented by diagonal density matrices).\n"
msgstr "Pengukuran umum bisa dijelaskan sebagai *channel* yang outputnya selalu berupa keadaan klasik (direpresentasikan oleh matriks densitas diagonal).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll restrict our attention to measurements having *finitely many* possible outcomes.\n"
"Although it is possible to define measurements with infinitely many possible outcomes, they're much less typically encountered in the context of computation and information processing, and they also require some additional mathematics (namely measure theory) to be properly formalized.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan membatasi perhatian pada pengukuran yang memiliki *finitely many* kemungkinan hasil.\n"
"Walaupun mungkin untuk mendefinisikan pengukuran dengan hasil tak terhingga, hal itu jarang ditemukan dalam konteks komputasi dan pemrosesan informasi, dan juga memerlukan matematika tambahan (yaitu teori ukuran) untuk diformalkan dengan benar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Our initial focus will be on so-called *destructive* measurements, where the output of the measurement is a classical measurement outcome alone — with no specification of the post-measurement quantum state of whatever system was measured.\n"
"Intuitively speaking, we can imagine that such a measurement destroys the quantum system itself, or that the system is immediately discarded once the measurement is made.\n"
"Later in the lesson we'll broaden our view and consider *non-destructive* measurements, where there's both a classical measurement outcome and a post-measurement quantum state of the measured system.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fokus awal kita adalah pada pengukuran *destruktif*, di mana output pengukuran hanya berupa hasil pengukuran klasik saja — tanpa spesifikasi keadaan kuantum pasca-pengukuran dari sistem yang diukur.\n"
"Secara intuitif, kita bisa bayangkan bahwa pengukuran semacam ini menghancurkan sistem kuantum itu sendiri, atau sistem langsung dibuang setelah pengukuran dilakukan.\n"
"Nanti dalam pelajaran ini kita akan memperluas pandangan dan mempertimbangkan pengukuran *non-destruktif*, di mana ada hasil pengukuran klasik sekaligus keadaan kuantum pasca-pengukuran dari sistem yang diukur.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measurements as collections of matrices {#measurements-as-collections-of-matrices}"
msgstr "Pengukuran sebagai kumpulan matriks {#measurements-as-collections-of-matrices}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose $\\mathsf{X}$ is a system that is to be measured, and assume for simplicity that the classical state set of $\\mathsf{X}$ is $\\{0,\\ldots, n-1\\}$ for some positive integer $n$, so that density matrices representing quantum states of $\\mathsf{X}$ are $n\\times n$ matrices.\n"
"We won't actually have much need to refer to the classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$, but it will be convenient to refer to $n$, the number of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"We'll also assume that the possible outcomes of the measurement are the integers $0,\\ldots,m-1$ for some positive integer $m$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalkan $\\mathsf{X}$ adalah sistem yang akan diukur, dan asumsikan untuk kesederhanaan bahwa himpunan keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{X}$ adalah $\\{0,\\ldots, n-1\\}$ untuk suatu bilangan bulat positif $n$, sehingga matriks densitas yang merepresentasikan keadaan kuantum $\\mathsf{X}$ adalah matriks $n\\times n$.\n"
"Kita sebenarnya tidak terlalu perlu merujuk ke keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{X}$, tapi akan berguna untuk merujuk $n$, yaitu jumlah keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Kita juga akan mengasumsikan bahwa kemungkinan hasil pengukuran adalah bilangan bulat $0,\\ldots,m-1$ untuk suatu bilangan bulat positif $m$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that we're just using these names to keep things simple;\n"
"it's straightforward to generalize everything that follows to other finite sets of classical states and measurement outcomes, renaming them as desired.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa kita hanya menggunakan nama-nama ini agar lebih sederhana;\n"
"mudah saja untuk menggeneralisasi semua yang berikut ke himpunan keadaan klasik dan hasil pengukuran terhingga lainnya, dengan mengganti namanya sesuai kebutuhan.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Projective measurements {#projective-measurements}"
msgstr "Pengukuran proyektif {#projective-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Recall that a *projective measurement* is described by a collection of *projection matrices* that sum to the identity matrix.\n"
"In symbols,\n"
msgstr ""
"Ingat bahwa *pengukuran proyektif* dijelaskan oleh kumpulan *matriks proyeksi* yang berjumlah sama dengan matriks identitas.\n"
"Dalam simbol,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\{\\Pi_0,\\ldots,\\Pi_{m-1}\\}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "describes a projective measurement of $\\mathsf{X}$ if each $\\Pi_a$ is an $n\\times n$ projection matrix and the following condition is met.\n"
msgstr "menjelaskan pengukuran proyektif dari $\\mathsf{X}$ jika setiap $\\Pi_a$ adalah matriks proyeksi $n\\times n$ dan kondisi berikut terpenuhi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Pi_0 + \\cdots + \\Pi_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When such a measurement is performed on a system $\\mathsf{X}$ while it's in a state described by some quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, each outcome $a$ is obtained with probability equal to $\\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\|^2$.\n"
"We also have that the post-measurement state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is obtained by normalizing the vector $\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, but we're ignoring the post-measurement state for now.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ketika pengukuran semacam itu dilakukan pada sistem $\\mathsf{X}$ saat berada dalam keadaan yang dijelaskan oleh vektor keadaan kuantum $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, setiap hasil $a$ diperoleh dengan probabilitas $\\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\|^2$.\n"
"Kita juga punya bahwa keadaan pasca-pengukuran $\\mathsf{X}$ diperoleh dengan menormalisasi vektor $\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, tapi kita mengabaikan keadaan pasca-pengukuran untuk saat ini.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is described by a density matrix $\\rho$ rather than a quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, then we can alternatively express the probability to obtain the outcome $a$ as $\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)$.\n"
msgstr "Jika keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$ dijelaskan oleh matriks densitas $\\rho$ daripada vektor keadaan kuantum $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$, maka kita bisa mengekspresikan probabilitas memperoleh hasil $a$ sebagai $\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If $\\rho = \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$ is a pure state, then the two expressions are equal:\n"
msgstr "Jika $\\rho = \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$ adalah keadaan murni, maka kedua ekspresi itu setara:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi \\vert)\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert \\Pi_a \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"= \\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\|^2.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\vert \\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi \\vert)\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"= \\langle \\psi \\vert \\Pi_a \\Pi_a \\vert \\psi \\rangle\n"
"= \\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\|^2.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we're using the cyclic property of the trace for the second equality, and for the third equality we're using the fact that each $\\Pi_a$ is a projection matrix, and therefore satisfies $\\Pi_a^2 = \\Pi_a$.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita menggunakan sifat siklik trace untuk persamaan kedua, dan untuk persamaan ketiga kita menggunakan fakta bahwa setiap $\\Pi_a$ adalah matriks proyeksi, sehingga memenuhi $\\Pi_a^2 = \\Pi_a$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In general, if $\\rho$ is a convex combination\n"
msgstr "Secara umum, jika $\\rho$ adalah kombinasi konveks\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "of pure states, then the expression $\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)$ coincides with the average probability for the outcome $a$, owing to the fact that this expression is linear in $\\rho$.\n"
msgstr "dari keadaan-keadaan murni, maka ekspresi $\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)$ bertepatan dengan probabilitas rata-rata untuk hasil $a$, berkat kenyataan bahwa ekspresi ini linier dalam $\\rho$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\|^2\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\rho)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\operatorname{Tr}(\\Pi_a \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k\\vert)\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} p_k \\|\\Pi_a\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle\\|^2\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "General measurements {#general-measurements}"
msgstr "Pengukuran umum {#general-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A mathematical description for general measurements is obtained by relaxing the definition of projective measurements.\n"
"Specifically, we allow the matrices in the collection describing the measurement to be arbitrary *positive semidefinite* matrices rather than projections.\n"
"(Projections are always positive semidefinite; they can alternatively be defined as positive semidefinite matrices whose eigenvalues are all either 0 or 1.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Deskripsi matematis untuk pengukuran umum diperoleh dengan melonggarkan definisi pengukuran proyektif.\n"
"Khususnya, kita mengizinkan matriks dalam kumpulan yang menjelaskan pengukuran menjadi matriks *positif semidefinit* yang sembarang, bukan hanya proyeksi.\n"
"(Proyeksi selalu positif semidefinit; mereka bisa juga didefinisikan sebagai matriks positif semidefinit yang nilai eigennya semua 0 atau 1.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In particular, a general measurement of a system $\\mathsf{X}$ having outcomes $0,\\ldots,m-1$ is specified by a collection of positive semidefinite matrices $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ whose rows and columns correspond to the classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ and that meet the condition\n"
msgstr "Secara khusus, pengukuran umum dari sistem $\\mathsf{X}$ dengan hasil $0,\\ldots,m-1$ ditentukan oleh kumpulan matriks positif semidefinit $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ yang baris dan kolomnya bersesuaian dengan keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{X}$ dan memenuhi kondisi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the system $\\mathsf{X}$ is measured while it is in a state described by the density matrix $\\rho$, then each outcome\n"
"$a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ appears with probability $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika sistem $\\mathsf{X}$ diukur saat berada dalam keadaan yang dijelaskan oleh matriks densitas $\\rho$, maka setiap hasil\n"
"$a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ muncul dengan probabilitas $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As we must naturally demand, the vector of outcome probabilities\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang harus kita tuntut secara alami, vektor probabilitas hasil\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl(\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho),\\ldots,\\operatorname{Tr}(P_{m-1} \\rho)\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl(\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho),\\ldots,\\operatorname{Tr}(P_{m-1} \\rho)\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"of a general measurement always forms a probability vector, for any choice of a density matrix $\\rho$.\n"
"The following two observations establish that this is the case.\n"
msgstr ""
"dari pengukuran umum selalu membentuk vektor probabilitas, untuk pilihan matriks densitas $\\rho$ apapun.\n"
"Dua observasi berikut menetapkan bahwa ini memang terjadi.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each value $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$ must be nonnegative, owing to the fact that the trace of the product of any two positive semidefinite matrices is always nonnegative:\n"
msgstr "Setiap nilai $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$ haruslah tak negatif, berkat fakta bahwa trace dari perkalian dua matriks positif semidefinit apapun selalu tak negatif:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   Q, R \\geq 0 \\; \\Rightarrow \\: \\operatorname{Tr}(QR) \\geq 0.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   Q, R \\geq 0 \\; \\Rightarrow \\: \\operatorname{Tr}(QR) \\geq 0.\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   One way to argue this fact is to use spectral decompositions of $Q$ and $R$ together with the cyclic property of the trace to express the trace of the product $QR$ as a sum of nonnegative real numbers, which must therefore be nonnegative.\n"
msgstr "   Salah satu cara untuk memargumenkan fakta ini adalah dengan menggunakan dekomposisi spektral dari $Q$ dan $R$ bersama sifat siklik trace untuk mengekspresikan trace dari perkalian $QR$ sebagai jumlah bilangan real tak negatif, yang harus tak negatif.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The condition $P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$ together with the linearity of the trace ensures that the probabilities sum to $1$.\n"
msgstr "Kondisi $P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$ bersama linearitas trace memastikan probabilitas berjumlah $1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\n"
"   = \\operatorname{Tr}\\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} P_a \\rho\\Biggr)\n"
"   = \\operatorname{Tr}(\\mathbb{I}\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho) = 1\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\n"
"   = \\operatorname{Tr}\\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} P_a \\rho\\Biggr)\n"
"   = \\operatorname{Tr}(\\mathbb{I}\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}(\\rho) = 1\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example 1: any projective measurement {#example-1-any-projective-measurement}"
msgstr "Contoh 1: pengukuran proyektif apapun {#example-1-any-projective-measurement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Projections are always positive semidefinite, so every projective measurement is an example of a general measurement.\n"
msgstr "Proyeksi selalu positif semidefinit, sehingga setiap pengukuran proyektif adalah contoh dari pengukuran umum.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For example, a standard basis measurement of a qubit can be represented by $\\{P_0,P_1\\}$ where\n"
msgstr "Misalnya, pengukuran basis standar dari sebuah qubit bisa direpresentasikan oleh $\\{P_0,P_1\\}$ di mana\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 = \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"P_1 = \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 = \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"P_1 = \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measuring a qubit in the state $\\rho$ results in outcome probabilities as follows.\n"
msgstr "Mengukur sebuah qubit dalam keadaan $\\rho$ menghasilkan probabilitas hasil sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Prob}(\\text{outcome} = 0)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\rho\\bigr) =\n"
"\\langle 0\\vert \\rho \\vert 0 \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Prob}(\\text{outcome} = 1)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\rho\\bigr) =\n"
"\\langle 1 \\vert \\rho \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Prob}(\\text{outcome} = 0)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\rho\\bigr) =\n"
"\\langle 0\\vert \\rho \\vert 0 \\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Prob}(\\text{outcome} = 1)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\rho\\bigr) =\n"
"\\langle 1 \\vert \\rho \\vert 1 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example 2: a non-projective qubit measurement {#example-2-a-non-projective-qubit-measurement}"
msgstr "Contoh 2: pengukuran qubit non-proyektif {#example-2-a-non-projective-qubit-measurement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose $\\mathsf{X}$ is a qubit, and define two matrices as follows.\n"
msgstr "Misalkan $\\mathsf{X}$ adalah sebuah qubit, dan definisikan dua matriks sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"P_1 =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"P_1 =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These are both positive semidefinite matrices: they're Hermitian, and in both cases the eigenvalues happen to be $1/2 \\pm \\sqrt{5}/6$, which are both positive.\n"
"We also have that $P_0 + P_1 = \\mathbb{I}$, and therefore $\\{P_0,P_1\\}$ describes a measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Keduanya adalah matriks positif semidefinit: keduanya Hermitian, dan dalam kedua kasus nilai eigen kebetulan adalah $1/2 \\pm \\sqrt{5}/6$, yang keduanya positif.\n"
"Kita juga punya $P_0 + P_1 = \\mathbb{I}$, dan oleh karena itu $\\{P_0,P_1\\}$ menjelaskan sebuah pengukuran.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is described by a density matrix $\\rho$ and we perform this measurement, then the probability of obtaining the outcome $0$ is $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho)$ and the probability of obtaining the outcome $1$ is\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho)$.\n"
"For instance, if $\\rho = \\vert + \\rangle \\langle + \\vert$ then the probabilities for the two outcomes $0$ and $1$ are as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$ dijelaskan oleh matriks densitas $\\rho$ dan kita melakukan pengukuran ini, maka probabilitas memperoleh hasil $0$ adalah $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho)$ dan probabilitas memperoleh hasil $1$ adalah\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho)$.\n"
"Misalnya, jika $\\rho = \\vert + \\rangle \\langle + \\vert$ maka probabilitas untuk dua hasil $0$ dan $1$ adalah sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\biggl(\\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"+ \\biggl(\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}  + \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{5}{6}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\biggl(\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"+ \\biggl(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}  + \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\\\\\n"
"& = 0 + \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{1}{6}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_0 \\rho)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\biggl(\\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"+ \\biggl(\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}  + \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\\\\\n"
"& = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{5}{6}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_1 \\rho)\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\left(\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\right)\\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\biggl(\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{3} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\n"
"+ \\biggl(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}  + \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{2}\\biggr)\\\\\n"
"& = 0 + \\frac{1}{6} = \\frac{1}{6}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example 3: tetrahedral measurement {#example-3-tetrahedral-measurement}"
msgstr "Contoh 3: pengukuran tetrahedral {#example-3-tetrahedral-measurement}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define four single-qubit quantum state vectors as follows.\n"
msgstr "Definisikan empat vektor keadaan kuantum satu-Qubit sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle & = \\vert 0 \\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_1\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_2\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} e^{2\\pi i/3} \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_3\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} e^{-2\\pi i/3} \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\phi_0\\rangle & = \\vert 0 \\rangle\\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_1\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_2\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} e^{2\\pi i/3} \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"\\vert\\phi_3\\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\vert 0 \\rangle + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} e^{-2\\pi i/3} \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These four states are sometimes known as *tetrahedral* states because they're vertices of a *regular tetrahedron* inscribed within the Bloch sphere.\n"
msgstr "Keempat keadaan ini kadang disebut keadaan *tetrahedral* karena mereka adalah titik sudut dari *tetrahedron beraturan* yang diinscripsi dalam bola Bloch.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Illustration of a tetrahedron inscribed in the Bloch sphere](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/general-measurements/tetrahedral-states.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Ilustrasi tetrahedron yang diinscripsi dalam bola Bloch](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-information/general-measurements/tetrahedral-states.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Cartesian coordinates of these four states on the Bloch sphere are\n"
msgstr "Koordinat Kartesius dari keempat keadaan ini pada bola Bloch adalah\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(0,0,1),\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\left( \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} , 0 , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\left( -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} , \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\left( -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} , -\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(0,0,1),\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\left( \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} , 0 , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\left( -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} , \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\left( -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} , -\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} , -\\frac{1}{3} \\right),\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which can be verified by expressing the density matrices representations of these states as linear combinations of Pauli matrices.\n"
msgstr "yang dapat diverifikasi dengan mengekspresikan representasi matriks densitas dari keadaan-keadaan ini sebagai kombinasi linier dari matriks Pauli.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_0 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_0 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\[1mm] 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_0 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_0 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"1 & 0\\\\[1mm] 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_1 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_1 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_1 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} + \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_2 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\sigma_y - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_2 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_2 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x + \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\sigma_y - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_3 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_3 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x - \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\sigma_y - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_3 \\rangle\\langle \\phi_3 \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{3} & -\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} + \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"-\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}} - \\frac{i}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{3}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\frac{\\mathbb{I} - \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\sigma_x - \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}} \\sigma_y - \\frac{1}{3}\\sigma_z}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "These four states are perfectly spread out on the Bloch sphere, each one equidistant from the other three and with the angles between any two of them always being the same.\n"
msgstr "Keempat keadaan ini tersebar merata di bola Bloch, masing-masing berjarak sama dari tiga lainnya dan sudut antara dua keadaan manapun selalu sama.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now let us define a measurement $\\{P_0,P_1,P_2,P_3\\}$ of a qubit by setting $P_a$ as follows for each $a=0,\\ldots,3$.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang mari kita definisikan pengukuran $\\{P_0,P_1,P_2,P_3\\}$ dari sebuah qubit dengan menetapkan $P_a$ sebagai berikut untuk setiap $a=0,\\ldots,3$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = \\frac{\\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert}{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = \\frac{\\vert\\phi_a\\rangle\\langle\\phi_a\\vert}{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can verify that this is a valid measurement as follows.\n"
msgstr "Kita dapat memverifikasi bahwa ini adalah pengukuran yang valid sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each $P_a$ is evidently positive semidefinite, being a pure state divided by one-half.\n"
"That is, each one is a Hermitian matrix and has one eigenvalue equal to $1/2$ and all other eigenvalues zero.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap $P_a$ jelas positif semidefinit, karena merupakan keadaan murni yang dibagi dua.\n"
"Artinya, masing-masing adalah matriks Hermitian dan memiliki satu nilai eigen sama dengan $1/2$ dan semua nilai eigen lainnya nol.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The sum of these matrices is the identity matrix: $P_0 + P_1 + P_2 + P_3 = \\mathbb{I}$.\n"
"The expressions of these matrices as linear combinations of Pauli matrices makes this straightforward to verify.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jumlah matriks-matriks ini adalah matriks identitas: $P_0 + P_1 + P_2 + P_3 = \\mathbb{I}.$\n"
"Ekspresi matriks-matriks ini sebagai kombinasi linier dari matriks Pauli memudahkan verifikasi ini.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Measurements as channels {#measurements-as-channels}"
msgstr "Pengukuran sebagai channel {#measurements-as-channels}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A second way to describe measurements in mathematical terms is as channels.\n"
msgstr "Cara kedua untuk mendeskripsikan pengukuran dalam istilah matematis adalah sebagai channel.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Classical information can be viewed as a special case of quantum information, insofar as we can identify probabilistic states with diagonal density matrices.\n"
"So, in operational terms, we can think about measurements as being channels whose inputs are matrices describing states of whatever system is being measured and whose outputs are *diagonal* density matrices describing the resulting distribution of measurement outcomes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Informasi klasik bisa dipandang sebagai kasus khusus dari informasi kuantum, sejauh kita dapat mengidentifikasi keadaan probabilistik dengan matriks densitas diagonal.\n"
"Jadi, dalam istilah operasional, kita dapat memandang pengukuran sebagai channel yang inputnya adalah matriks yang mendeskripsikan keadaan sistem apapun yang diukur dan outputnya adalah matriks densitas *diagonal* yang mendeskripsikan distribusi hasil pengukuran yang dihasilkan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll see shortly that any channel having this property can always be written in a simple, canonical form that ties directly to the description of measurements as collections of positive semidefinite matrices.\n"
"Conversely, given an arbitrary measurement as a collection of matrices, there's always a valid channel having the diagonal output property that describes the given measurement as suggested in the previous paragraph.\n"
"Putting these observations together, we find that the two descriptions of general measurements are equivalent.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita akan segera melihat bahwa setiap channel yang memiliki sifat ini selalu bisa ditulis dalam bentuk kanonik sederhana yang terhubung langsung dengan deskripsi pengukuran sebagai kumpulan matriks positif semidefinit.\n"
"Sebaliknya, untuk setiap pengukuran umum sebagai kumpulan matriks, selalu ada channel valid dengan sifat output diagonal yang mendeskripsikan pengukuran yang diberikan seperti yang disarankan di paragraf sebelumnya.\n"
"Dengan menggabungkan observasi-observasi ini, kita menemukan bahwa kedua deskripsi pengukuran umum itu setara.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before proceeding further, let's be more precise about the measurement, how we're viewing it as a channel, and what assumptions we're making about it.\n"
msgstr "Sebelum melanjutkan, mari kita lebih tepat tentang pengukuran, bagaimana kita memandangnya sebagai channel, dan asumsi apa yang kita buat.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As before, we'll suppose that $\\mathsf{X}$ is the system to be measured, and that the possible outcomes of the measurement are the integers $0,\\ldots,m-1$ for some positive integer $m$.\n"
"We let $\\mathsf{Y}$ be the system that stores measurement outcomes, so its classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, and we represent the measurement as a channel named $\\Phi$ from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
"Our assumption is that $\\mathsf{Y}$ is *classical* — which is to say that no matter what state we start with for $\\mathsf{X}$, the state of $\\mathsf{Y}$ we obtain is represented by a diagonal density matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti sebelumnya, kita akan asumsikan bahwa $\\mathsf{X}$ adalah sistem yang akan diukur, dan bahwa kemungkinan hasil pengukuran adalah bilangan bulat $0,\\ldots,m-1$ untuk suatu bilangan bulat positif $m$.\n"
"Kita biarkan $\\mathsf{Y}$ menjadi sistem yang menyimpan hasil pengukuran, sehingga himpunan keadaan klasiknya adalah $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, dan kita merepresentasikan pengukuran sebagai channel bernama $\\Phi$ dari $\\mathsf{X}$ ke $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
"Asumsi kita adalah bahwa $\\mathsf{Y}$ bersifat *klasik* — artinya tidak peduli keadaan awal $\\mathsf{X}$ apapun, keadaan $\\mathsf{Y}$ yang kita peroleh direpresentasikan oleh matriks densitas diagonal.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can express in mathematical terms that the output of $\\Phi$ is always diagonal in the following way.\n"
"First define the completely dephasing channel $\\Delta_m$ on $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita dapat mengekspresikan dalam istilah matematis bahwa output $\\Phi$ selalu diagonal dengan cara berikut.\n"
"Pertama definisikan channel completely dephasing $\\Delta_m$ pada $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta_m(\\sigma) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert \\sigma \\vert a\\rangle \\,\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Delta_m(\\sigma) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert \\sigma \\vert a\\rangle \\,\\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This channel is analogous to the completely dephasing qubit channel $\\Delta$ from the previous lesson.\n"
"As a linear mapping, it zeros out all of the off-diagonal entries of an input matrix and leaves the diagonal alone.\n"
msgstr ""
"Channel ini analog dengan channel completely dephasing qubit $\\Delta$ dari pelajaran sebelumnya.\n"
"Sebagai pemetaan linier, channel ini mengnolkan semua entri off-diagonal dari matriks input dan membiarkan diagonal tetap.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"And now, a simple way to express that a given density matrix $\\sigma$ is diagonal is by the equation\n"
"$\\sigma = \\Delta_m(\\sigma)$.\n"
"In words, zeroing out all of the off-diagonal entries of a density matrix has no effect if and only if the off-diagonal entries were all zero to begin with.\n"
"The channel $\\Phi$ therefore satisfies our assumption — that $\\mathsf{Y}$ is classical — if and only if\n"
msgstr ""
"Dan sekarang, cara sederhana untuk mengekspresikan bahwa matriks densitas $\\sigma$ yang diberikan itu diagonal adalah melalui persamaan\n"
"$\\sigma = \\Delta_m(\\sigma)$.\n"
"Dengan kata lain, mengnolkan semua entri off-diagonal dari matriks densitas tidak berpengaruh jika dan hanya jika entri off-diagonal memang sudah nol sejak awal.\n"
"Oleh karena itu channel $\\Phi$ memenuhi asumsi kita — bahwa $\\mathsf{Y}$ bersifat klasik — jika dan hanya jika\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\Delta_m(\\Phi(\\rho))\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\Delta_m(\\Phi(\\rho))\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for every density matrix $\\rho$ representing a state of $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
msgstr "untuk setiap matriks densitas $\\rho$ yang merepresentasikan keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Equivalence of the formulations {#equivalence-of-the-formulations}"
msgstr "Kesetaraan formulasi {#equivalence-of-the-formulations}"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Channels to matrices {#channels-to-matrices}"
msgstr "Dari channel ke matriks {#channels-to-matrices}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose that we have a channel from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y}$ with the property that\n"
msgstr "Misalkan kita punya channel dari $\\mathsf{X}$ ke $\\mathsf{Y}$ dengan sifat bahwa\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for every density matrix $\\rho$.\n"
"This may alternatively be expressed as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"untuk setiap matriks densitas $\\rho$.\n"
"Ini bisa juga diekspresikan sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert \\Phi(\\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert \\Phi(\\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Like all channels, we can express $\\Phi$ in Kraus form for some way of choosing Kraus matrices\n"
"$A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seperti semua channel, kita bisa mengekspresikan $\\Phi$ dalam bentuk Kraus untuk suatu pilihan matriks Kraus\n"
"$A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This provides us with an alternative expression for the diagonal entries of $\\Phi(\\rho)\\!:$\n"
msgstr "Ini memberi kita ekspresi alternatif untuk entri diagonal $\\Phi(\\rho)\\!:$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\Phi(\\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle a \\vert A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k \\rho\\bigr)\\\\\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(P_a\\rho\\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\Phi(\\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle a \\vert A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k \\rho\\bigr)\\\\\n"
"& = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(P_a\\rho\\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "for\n"
msgstr "untuk\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_a = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, for these same matrices $P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}$ we can express the channel $\\Phi$ as follows.\n"
msgstr "Dengan demikian, untuk matriks-matriks $P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}$ yang sama kita bisa mengekspresikan channel $\\Phi$ sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho) \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This expression is consistent with our description of general measurements in terms of matrices, as we see each measurement outcome appearing with probability $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$.\n"
msgstr "Ekspresi ini konsisten dengan deskripsi pengukuran umum kita dalam hal matriks, karena kita melihat setiap hasil pengukuran muncul dengan probabilitas $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's observe that the two properties required of the collection of matrices $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ to describe a general measurement are indeed satisfied.\n"
"The first property is that they're all positive semidefinite matrices.\n"
"One way to see this is to observe that, for every vector $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ having entries in correspondence with the classical state of $\\mathsf{X}$ we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Sekarang mari kita amati bahwa dua sifat yang diperlukan dari kumpulan matriks $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ untuk mendeskripsikan pengukuran umum memang terpenuhi.\n"
"Sifat pertama adalah bahwa semuanya adalah matriks positif semidefinit.\n"
"Salah satu cara untuk melihat ini adalah dengan mengamati bahwa, untuk setiap vektor $\\vert \\psi\\rangle$ yang entri-entrinya bersesuaian dengan keadaan klasik $\\mathsf{X}$ kita punya\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert P_a \\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle \\psi \\vert A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k\\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"=  \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\bigl\\vert\\langle a \\vert A_k\\vert \\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\vert^2 \\geq 0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi \\vert P_a \\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle \\psi \\vert A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k\\vert \\psi\\rangle\n"
"=  \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\bigl\\vert\\langle a \\vert A_k\\vert \\psi\\rangle\\bigr\\vert^2 \\geq 0.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The second property is that if we sum these matrices we get the identity matrix.\n"
msgstr "Sifat kedua adalah bahwa jika kita menjumlahkan matriks-matriks ini kita mendapatkan matriks identitas.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} P_a\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\\Biggr) A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} P_a\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} \\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\\Biggr) A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\\\\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The last equality follows from the fact that $\\Phi$ is a channel, so its Kraus matrices must satisfy this condition.\n"
msgstr "Persamaan terakhir mengikuti fakta bahwa $\\Phi$ adalah channel, sehingga matriks Kraus-nya harus memenuhi kondisi ini.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Matrices to channels {#matrices-to-channels}"
msgstr "Dari matriks ke channel {#matrices-to-channels}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now let's verify that for any collection $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ of positive semidefinite matrices satisfying $P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$, the mapping defined by\n"
msgstr "Sekarang mari kita verifikasi bahwa untuk kumpulan $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ matriks positif semidefinit manapun yang memenuhi $P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$, pemetaan yang didefinisikan oleh\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho) \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho) \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "is indeed a valid channel from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"
msgstr "memang merupakan channel yang valid dari $\\mathsf{X}$ ke $\\mathsf{Y}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One way to do this is to compute the Choi representation of this mapping.\n"
msgstr "Salah satu cara untuk melakukan ini adalah dengan menghitung representasi Choi dari pemetaan ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"J(\\Phi) & = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes \\Phi(\\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert) \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle b \\vert P_a^T \\vert c \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes\n"
"\\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a^T \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"J(\\Phi) & = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes \\Phi(\\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b \\rangle \\langle c \\vert) \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle b \\vert P_a^T \\vert c \\rangle \\langle c \\vert \\otimes\n"
"\\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a^T \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle\\langle a\\vert\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The transpose of each $P_a$ is introduced for the third equality because\n"
msgstr "Transpose dari setiap $P_a$ diperkenalkan untuk persamaan ketiga karena\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle c \\vert P_a \\vert b\\rangle = \\langle b \\vert P_a^T \\vert c\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle c \\vert P_a \\vert b\\rangle = \\langle b \\vert P_a^T \\vert c\\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This allows for the expressions $\\vert b \\rangle \\langle b \\vert$ and $\\vert c \\rangle \\langle c \\vert$ to appear, which simplify to the identity matrix upon summing over $b$ and $c$, respectively.\n"
msgstr "Ini memungkinkan ekspresi $\\vert b \\rangle \\langle b \\vert$ dan $\\vert c \\rangle \\langle c \\vert$ untuk muncul, yang menyederhanakan menjadi matriks identitas ketika dijumlahkan atas $b$ dan $c$, masing-masing.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By the assumption that $P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}$ are positive semidefinite, so too are $P_0^{T},\\ldots,P_{m-1}^{T}$.\n"
"In particular, transposing a Hermitian matrix results in another Hermitian matrix, and the eigenvalues of any square matrix and its transpose always agree.\n"
"It follows that $J(\\Phi)$ is positive semidefinite.\n"
"Tracing out the output system $\\mathsf{Y}$ (which is the system on the right) yields\n"
msgstr ""
"Berdasarkan asumsi bahwa $P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}$ positif semidefinit, demikian pula $P_0^{T},\\ldots,P_{m-1}^{T}$.\n"
"Khususnya, mentranspose matriks Hermitian menghasilkan matriks Hermitian lainnya, dan nilai eigen dari matriks kuadrat apapun dan transposenya selalu sama.\n"
"Mengikuti hal ini$,J(\\Phi)$ adalah positif semidefinit.\n"
"Menelusuri keluar sistem output $\\mathsf{Y}$ (yang merupakan sistem di sebelah kanan) menghasilkan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and so we conclude that $\\Phi$ is a channel.\n"
msgstr "sehingga kita simpulkan bahwa $\\Phi$ adalah sebuah channel.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Partial measurements {#partial-measurements}"
msgstr "Pengukuran parsial {#partial-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that we have multiple systems that are collectively in a quantum state, and a general measurement is performed on one of the systems.\n"
"This results in one of the measurement outcomes, selected at random according to probabilities determined by the measurement and the state of the system prior to the measurement.\n"
"The resulting state of the remaining systems will then, in general, depend on which measurement outcome was obtained.\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalkan kita punya beberapa sistem yang secara kolektif berada dalam suatu keadaan kuantum, dan pengukuran umum dilakukan pada salah satu sistem tersebut.\n"
"Hasilnya adalah salah satu hasil pengukuran, dipilih secara acak sesuai dengan probabilitas yang ditentukan oleh pengukuran dan keadaan sistem sebelum pengukuran.\n"
"Keadaan yang dihasilkan dari sistem-sistem yang tersisa kemudian, pada umumnya, bergantung pada hasil pengukuran mana yang diperoleh.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's examine how this works for a pair of systems $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ when the system $\\mathsf{X}$ is measured.\n"
"(We're naming the system on the right $\\mathsf{Z}$ because we'll take $\\mathsf{Y}$ to be a system representing the classical output of the measurement when we view it as a channel.)\n"
"We can then easily generalize to the situation in which the systems are swapped as well as to three or more systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita periksa bagaimana ini bekerja untuk sepasang sistem $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ ketika sistem $\\mathsf{X}$ diukur.\n"
"(Kita menamakan sistem di sebelah kanan $\\mathsf{Z}$ karena kita akan mengambil $\\mathsf{Y}$ sebagai sistem yang merepresentasikan keluaran klasik dari pengukuran ketika kita memandangnya sebagai channel.)\n"
"Kita kemudian bisa dengan mudah menggeneralisasi ke situasi di mana sistem-sistem tersebut dibalik urutannya maupun ke tiga sistem atau lebih.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose the state of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ prior to the measurement is described by a density matrix $\\rho$, which we can write as follows.\n"
msgstr "Misalkan keadaan $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ sebelum pengukuran dijelaskan oleh matriks densitas $\\rho$, yang bisa kita tulis sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this expression we're assuming the classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ are $0,\\ldots,n-1$.\n"
msgstr "Dalam ekspresi ini kita mengasumsikan keadaan klasik dari $\\mathsf{X}$ adalah $0,\\ldots,n-1$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll assume that the measurement itself is described by the collection of matrices\n"
"$\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$.\n"
"This measurement may alternatively be described as a channel $\\Phi$ from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y}$, where $\\mathsf{Y}$ is a new system having classical state set $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$.\n"
"Specifically, the action of this channel can be expressed as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita asumsikan bahwa pengukuran itu sendiri dijelaskan oleh kumpulan matriks\n"
"$\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$.\n"
"Pengukuran ini bisa secara alternatif dijelaskan sebagai channel $\\Phi$ dari $\\mathsf{X}$ ke $\\mathsf{Y}$, di mana $\\mathsf{Y}$ adalah sistem baru yang memiliki himpunan keadaan klasik $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$.\n"
"Secara khusus, aksi channel ini bisa diekspresikan sebagai berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\xi) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\xi)\\, \\vert a \\rangle \\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\xi) = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\xi)\\, \\vert a \\rangle \\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Outcome probabilities {#outcome-probabilities}"
msgstr "Probabilitas hasil {#outcome-probabilities}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We're considering a measurement of the system $\\mathsf{X}$, so the probabilities with which different measurement outcomes are obtained can depend only on $\\rho_{\\mathsf{X}}$, the reduced state of $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"In particular, the probability for each outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ to appear can be expressed in three equivalent ways.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita mempertimbangkan pengukuran sistem $\\mathsf{X}$, sehingga probabilitas diperolehnya berbagai hasil pengukuran hanya bergantung pada $\\rho_{\\mathsf{X}}$, keadaan tereduksi dari $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Secara khusus, probabilitas untuk setiap hasil $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ yang muncul bisa diekspresikan dalam tiga cara yang ekuivalen.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( P_a \\rho_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigr) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( P_a \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Z}}(\\rho)\\bigr) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( (P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( P_a \\rho_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigr) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( P_a \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Z}}(\\rho)\\bigr) =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl( (P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first expression naturally represents the probability to obtain the outcome $a$ based on what we already know about measurements of a single system.\n"
"To get the second expression we're simply using the definition $\\rho_{\\mathsf{X}} = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Z}}(\\rho)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ekspresi pertama secara alami merepresentasikan probabilitas untuk memperoleh hasil $a$ berdasarkan apa yang sudah kita ketahui tentang pengukuran sistem tunggal.\n"
"Untuk mendapatkan ekspresi kedua kita cukup menggunakan definisi $\\rho_{\\mathsf{X}} = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Z}}(\\rho)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To get the third expression requires more thought — and learners are encouraged to convince themselves that it is true.\n"
"Here's a hint: The equivalence between the second and third expressions does not depend on $\\rho$ being a density matrix or on each $P_a$ being positive semidefinite. Try showing it first for tensor products of the form $\\rho = M\\otimes N$ and then conclude that it must be true in general by linearity.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mendapatkan ekspresi ketiga memerlukan pemikiran lebih — dan para pelajar didorong untuk meyakinkan diri mereka sendiri bahwa hal itu benar.\n"
"Berikut petunjuknya: Ekuivalensi antara ekspresi kedua dan ketiga tidak bergantung pada $\\rho$ yang merupakan matriks densitas atau pada setiap $P_a$ yang bersifat positif semidefinit. Coba tunjukkan pertama untuk hasil kali tensor berbentuk $\\rho = M\\otimes N$ dan kemudian simpulkan bahwa hal itu harus benar secara umum dengan linearitas.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"While the equivalence of the first and third expressions in the previous equation may not be immediate, it does make sense.\n"
"Starting from a measurement on $\\mathsf{X}$, we're effectively defining a measurement of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$, where we simply throw away $\\mathsf{Z}$ and measure $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Like all measurements, this new measurement can be described by a collection of matrices, and it's not surprising that this measurement is described by the collection\n"
msgstr ""
"Meskipun ekuivalensi antara ekspresi pertama dan ketiga dalam persamaan sebelumnya mungkin tidak langsung terlihat, hal itu masuk akal.\n"
"Dimulai dari pengukuran pada $\\mathsf{X}$, kita secara efektif mendefinisikan pengukuran dari $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$, di mana kita cukup membuang $\\mathsf{Z}$ dan mengukur $\\mathsf{X}$.\n"
"Seperti semua pengukuran, pengukuran baru ini bisa dijelaskan oleh kumpulan matriks, dan tidak mengejutkan bahwa pengukuran ini dijelaskan oleh kumpulan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\{P_0\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}, \\ldots, P_{m-1}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}\\}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\{P_0\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}, \\ldots, P_{m-1}\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}\\}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "States conditioned on measurement outcomes {#states-conditioned-on-measurement-outcomes}"
msgstr "Keadaan terkondisi pada hasil pengukuran {#states-conditioned-on-measurement-outcomes}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If we want to determine not only the probabilities for the different outcomes but also the resulting state of $\\mathsf{Z}$ conditioned on each measurement outcome, we can look to the channel description of the measurement.\n"
"In particular, let's examine the state we get when we apply $\\Phi$ to $\\mathsf{X}$ and do nothing to $\\mathsf{Z}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Jika kita ingin menentukan tidak hanya probabilitas untuk berbagai hasil tetapi juga keadaan yang dihasilkan dari $\\mathsf{Z}$ terkondisi pada setiap hasil pengukuran, kita bisa melihat ke deskripsi channel dari pengukuran.\n"
"Secara khusus, mari kita periksa keadaan yang kita dapatkan ketika kita menerapkan $\\Phi$ pada $\\mathsf{X}$ dan tidak melakukan apa-apa pada $\\mathsf{Z}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  (\\Phi\\otimes\\operatorname{Id}_{\\mathsf{Z}})(\\rho)\n"
"  & = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\Phi(\\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert) \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert)\n"
"    \\,\\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1}\n"
"    \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert) \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes\n"
"    \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}})\n"
"    (\\vert b\\rangle\\langle  c\\vert\\otimes\\rho_{b,c})\\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes\n"
"    \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho\\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  (\\Phi\\otimes\\operatorname{Id}_{\\mathsf{Z}})(\\rho)\n"
"  & = \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\Phi(\\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert) \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert)\n"
"    \\,\\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1}\n"
"    \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\vert b\\rangle\\langle c\\vert) \\rho_{b,c}\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes\n"
"    \\sum_{b,c = 0}^{n-1} \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}})\n"
"    (\\vert b\\rangle\\langle  c\\vert\\otimes\\rho_{b,c})\\bigr)\\\\\n"
"  & = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes\n"
"    \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho\\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that this is a density matrix by virtue of the fact that $\\Phi$ is a channel, so each matrix\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)$ is necessarily positive semidefinite.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahwa ini adalah matriks densitas karena fakta bahwa $\\Phi$ adalah channel, sehingga setiap matriks\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)$ pastilah positif semidefinit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One final step transforms this expression into one that reveals what we're looking for.\n"
msgstr "Satu langkah akhir mengubah ekspresi ini menjadi satu yang mengungkapkan apa yang kita cari.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\\,\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\\,\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is an example of a *classical-quantum state*,\n"
msgstr "Ini adalah contoh dari *keadaan klasik-kuantum*,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} p(a)\\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert \\otimes \\sigma_a,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} p(a)\\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a\\vert \\otimes \\sigma_a,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"like we saw in the *Density matrices* lesson.\n"
"For each measurement outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, we have with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"seperti yang kita lihat dalam pelajaran *Matriks densitas*.\n"
"Untuk setiap hasil pengukuran $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$, kita memiliki dengan probabilitas\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "that $\\mathsf{Y}$ is in the classical state $\\vert a \\rangle \\langle a \\vert$ and $\\mathsf{Z}$ is in the state\n"
msgstr "bahwa $\\mathsf{Y}$ berada dalam keadaan klasik $\\vert a \\rangle \\langle a \\vert$ dan $\\mathsf{Z}$ berada dalam keadaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma_a = \\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma_a = \\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)}.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "That is, this is the density matrix we obtain by normalizing\n"
msgstr "Artinya, ini adalah matriks densitas yang kita peroleh dengan menormalisasi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"by dividing it by its trace.\n"
"(Formally speaking, the state $\\sigma_a$ is only defined when the probability $p(a)$ is nonzero;\n"
"when $p(a) = 0$ this state is irrelevant, for it refers to a discrete event that occurs with probability zero.)\n"
msgstr ""
"dengan membaginya dengan tracenya.\n"
"(Secara formal, keadaan $\\sigma_a$ hanya terdefinisi ketika probabilitas $p(a)$ tidak nol;\n"
"ketika $p(a) = 0$ keadaan ini tidak relevan, karena mengacu pada peristiwa diskret yang terjadi dengan probabilitas nol.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Naturally, the outcome probabilities are consistent with our previous observations.\n"
msgstr "Secara alami, probabilitas hasil konsisten dengan pengamatan kita sebelumnya.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In summary, this is what happens when the measurement $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ is performed on $\\mathsf{X}$ when $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ is in the state $\\rho$.\n"
msgstr "Ringkasnya, inilah yang terjadi ketika pengukuran $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ dilakukan pada $\\mathsf{X}$ ketika $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Z})$ berada dalam keadaan $\\rho$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Each outcome $a$ appears with probability $p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)$.\n"
msgstr "Setiap hasil $a$ muncul dengan probabilitas $p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conditioned on obtaining the outcome $a$, the state of $\\mathsf{Z}$ is then represented by the density matrix $\\sigma_a$ shown in the equation $(2)$, which is obtained by normalizing $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)$.\n"
msgstr "Terkondisi pada diperolehnya hasil $a$, keadaan $\\mathsf{Z}$ kemudian direpresentasikan oleh matriks densitas $\\sigma_a$ yang ditunjukkan dalam persamaan $(2)$, yang diperoleh dengan menormalisasi $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}}\\bigl((P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Z}}) \\rho)$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generalization {#generalization}"
msgstr "Generalisasi {#generalization}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can adapt this description to other situations, such as when the ordering of the systems is reversed or when there are three or more systems.\n"
"Conceptually it is straightforward, although it can become cumbersome to write down the formulas.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita bisa mengadaptasi deskripsi ini ke situasi lain, seperti ketika urutan sistem dibalik atau ketika ada tiga sistem atau lebih.\n"
"Secara konseptual ini mudah, meskipun bisa menjadi rumit untuk menuliskan rumus-rumusnya.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In general, if we have $r$ systems $\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r$, the state of the compound system $(\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r)$ is $\\rho$, and the measurement $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ is performed on $\\mathsf{X}_k$, the following happens.\n"
msgstr "Secara umum, jika kita memiliki $r$ sistem $\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r$, keadaan sistem gabungan $(\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r)$ adalah $\\rho$, dan pengukuran $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ dilakukan pada $\\mathsf{X}_k$, hal berikut terjadi.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each outcome $a$ appears with probability\n"
"$$\n"
"p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap hasil $a$ muncul dengan probabilitas\n"
"$$\n"
"p(a) = \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Conditioned on obtaining the outcome $a$, the state of $(\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_{k-1},\\mathsf{X}_{k+1},\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r)$ is then represented by the following density matrix.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}_k}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Terkondisi pada diperolehnya hasil $a$, keadaan $(\\mathsf{X}_1,\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_{k-1},\\mathsf{X}_{k+1},\\ldots,\\mathsf{X}_r)$ kemudian direpresentasikan oleh matriks densitas berikut.\n"
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{X}_k}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr)}{\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl((\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_1}\\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k-1}} \\otimes P_a \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_{k+1}} \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}_r}) \\rho\\bigr)}\n"
"$$\n"
